WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:07.149
Once Spider-Man joined the MCU back in 2016's
Captain America: Civil War, it seemed like

00:00:07.149 --> 00:00:11.030
we'd entered a bold new era of cinematic web
slinging.

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:16.350
Actor Tom Holland is a young man, portraying
a high-school aged Peter Parker still trying

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:19.240
to figure out how to put the Man in Spider-Man.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:24.650
So in the lead-up to Avengers: Infinity War,
everyone expected to see Spider-Man doing

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:29.710
some pretty cool stuff, suiting up as the
Iron Spider to take on Thanos and his gang

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:30.710
of creeps.

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:35.550
We should probably pause the video now to
let you know that there are some Thanos-sized

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:36.920
spoilers ahead.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:37.920
Still with us?

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:38.920
Good.

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:43.720
Even though the credits have rolled and we've
all reserved our seats for Avengers 4 in 2019,

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:48.329
we're still trying to process everything we
saw in Avengers: Infinity War.

00:00:48.329 --> 00:00:54.570
No one, seriously, no one expected to to leave
the theater bawling our eyes out at the tragic

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:58.420
death of young Peter Parker, the amazingly
dead Spider-Man.

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:02.710
Of course, he's not the only casualty of Thanos'
mad quest.

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:08.700
The conclusion to Marvel Studios' record-setting
team-up movie might be the most despairing

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:14.139
sequence ever filmed for a summer blockbuster,
as the movie ends with half the population

00:01:14.139 --> 00:01:18.200
of the entire universe being blinked out of
existence.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:23.280
Watching Earth's mightiest heroes and almost
all of the Guardians of the Galaxy being turned

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:26.959
to ash and disappearing is a haunting thing
to experience.

00:01:26.959 --> 00:01:32.329
But the most affecting moment of the sequence
comes from Tom Holland's Spider-Man, who gets

00:01:32.329 --> 00:01:37.409
a horrifying moment to realize what's going
on before he collapses and fades away.

00:01:37.409 --> 00:01:43.270
He pleads for his life, and, in Tony Stark's
arms, he uses his last words to apologize

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:46.079
to his surrogate father for not doing better.

00:01:46.079 --> 00:01:50.159
And before Stark can so much as tell him to
knock it off, he's gone.

00:01:50.159 --> 00:01:54.840
Seeing the teenage Spider-Man fade out of
existence is the moment that takes the movie's

00:01:54.840 --> 00:02:00.489
climax from sad to heart-wrenching, making
for a final reel that seems to be bringing

00:02:00.489 --> 00:02:02.740
many moviegoers to tears.

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:07.450
Of course, once the lights came back on in
the theater, you probably started to realize

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:12.280
that, well, as sad as it was to watch Spidey
go, he'll definitely be back.

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:13.300
Here's why.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:18.970
A sequel to Spider-Man: Homecoming was announced
in late 2016, and is set to begin shooting

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:20.740
in July, 2018.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:26.130
So even if Peter's tragic death in Infinity
War made you cry into your popcorn, you can

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:30.250
rest assured he'll be back in time to star
in his own follow-up.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:35.360
But if you really want to go deep on why you
haven't seen the last of movie Spidey, just

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:38.010
look to the pages of Marvel comic books.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:44.590
In the first issue of Infinity Gauntlet, the
1991 six-issue series on which much of Infinity

00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:50.630
War is based, Spider-Man is one of the first
Marvel heroes to realize something seriously

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:52.450
bad is going down.

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:56.980
Joining up with the rest of the world's remaining
heroes and taking the fight to outer space,

00:02:56.980 --> 00:03:01.420
he stays in the game against Thanos for almost
the entire battle.

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:04.660
That's a pretty big change from what we got
in the film, right?

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:09.860
So why did Infinity War make that change,
and take out Spider-Man with Thanos' snap?

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:15.340
Well, as strong as Spider-Man is, he's not
actually essential to winning the battle.

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:20.530
In the comics, the endgame of the fight takes
place after the clock gets turned back 24

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:24.180
hours, landing Spider-Man back in New York
City.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:29.780
Afterwards, the final fight is led by Marvel's
most mystical members and its heaviest hitters,

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:36.100
with Dr. Strange, Thor, Drax, Hulk, Thanos'
brother Starfox, and Adam Warlock teaming

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:41.900
up with an epic alliance of Marvel's cosmic
entities to finish off the fight.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:46.000
Spidey's off to the side, doing whatever a
spider, uh, does.

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:51.040
Let's just face it.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:56.630
There's not much Spider-Man can do in a battle
between gods, and erasing him from existence

00:03:56.630 --> 00:04:02.150
is a much more impactful way to end Infinity
War than just benching him in the fourth quarter,

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:03.170
like in the comics.

00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:04.330
That's lame.

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:06.290
This is drama.

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:08.330
So dry your eyes, true believers.

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:14.000
Avengers: Infinity War may be one of the most
audacious summer movies in recent memory,

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:17.729
but nobody's crazy enough to really squash
Spider-Man.

00:04:17.729 --> 00:04:19.840
Not until he does this, at least…

00:04:21.949 --> 00:04:23.080
Yikes.

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:24.220
Thanks for watching!

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:27.430
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

